        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete author Theorem1.1 proof is supplied, including uniform Luna slice reduction, all new local derivative estimates, reduced-admissible induction8.2 and the two global interval cases. Select a finite group representation on a finite-dimensional complex V with a minimal homogeneous basic-invariant system sigma_j of degrees d_j and maximal degree d>=2. The curve on a bounded open interval extends with C^(d-1),1 coordinate regularity to its closure and takes values in sigma(V); every continuous lift is absolutely continuous with the exact1.1 Lp derivative bound for1<=p<d/(d-1). The constant depends on the representation, chosen invariants, interval length and p; endpoint-independent strengthening and the critical weak-Lp question are not claimed. Prior radical derivative bounds, Luna slices, interpolation and prepared-cover theorem are identified source background. The source elementary slice-degree observation4.5 points to the existing polynomial-generator/Taylor-minimality argument, explicitly written as Lemma3 on physical page12 of prior arXiv1406.2485v3; this was checked for the cited dependency scope, not reproduced or independently rederived. The full new group-order lifting induction and gluing core is written in this article. Multivariable and Q-valued variants are not separately counted."
      },
